  "result": "I fixed the inverted plan check in `src/server/services/search-service.ts`, but I haven't run the tests.\n\nThe colon check in `search()` rejected the query when `advanced_search` was enabled instead of when it was disabled. That is why the customer on the plan with field-scoped search was blocked and the customer without it never was. The condition is now `input.q.includes(\":\") && !advanced`.\n\nI also read `isEnabled` in `src/lib/feature-flags.ts`, and it correctly returns true for enterprise plans and for orgs with an override. Plain keyword searches don't contain a colon, so they behave as before.",
